| SWE.1 | Software Requirements Analysis | F | **CL1** |
| SWE.2 | Software Architectural Design | F | **CL1** |
| SWE.3 | Software Detailed Design and Unit Construction | F | **CL1** |
| SWE.4 | Software Unit Verification | L ⚠ | **CL1 ⚠** |
| SWE.5 | Software Integration and Integration Testing | F | **CL1** |
| SWE.6 | Software Qualification Testing | F | **CL1** |
| MAN.3 | Project Management | L ⚠ | **CL1 ⚠** |
| MAN.5 | Risk Management | F | **CL1** |
| MAN.6 | Measurement | L ⚠ | **CL1 ⚠** |
| SUP.1 | Quality Assurance | L ⚠ | **CL1 ⚠** |
| SUP.8 | Configuration Management | F | **CL1** |
| SUP.9 | Problem Resolution Management | L | **CL1** |
| SUP.10 | Change Request Management | F | **CL1** |

All 13 processes achieve CL1. No process achieves CL2 — not because the technical work is weak, but because **PA 2.1 and PA 2.2 are universally Partially achieved** across the board: no document has a version/revision/approval header, and no formal review execution records exist.

---

### Assessment 1 Finding Status: CONFIRMED RESOLVED

All 18 CRs from Assessment 1 are closed. The three Critical findings (governance gap, missing derived requirements, no CR process) are fully resolved.

---

### Assessment 2 New Findings

**2 Major Findings:**
- **MF2-01** — UT-006/007/009 link to SWE-004 instead of SWE-007, creating false traceability gaps in the unit test report
- **MF2-02** — Corrective-action-log statuses are stale: CA-06 still "In-Progress", CA-07 still "Open", all P2 CAs still "Assigned" — the official CA log does not reflect actual closure

**7 Observations** covering: document version headers (OB2-01, universal CL2 blocker), no review records (OB2-02), no coverage measurement executed (OB2-03), attendance placeholders in status review (OB2-04), M1 date inconsistency and M6 effort gap (OB2-05), missing `.clang-format` CM item (OB2-06), no QA audit execution records (OB2-07), problem log semantic contradiction (OB2-08)

